  nodeAbstract: 
  nodeTextLayers:
  - GLP1-R is a transmembrane protein, meaning that it spans the entire thickness
    of the cell membrane.
  - GLP1-R has 7 transmembrane helices. These helices form a peptide-binding pocket
    that GLP1 sits in.
  - Many transmembrane proteins function as gateways to allow the transport of specific
    substances or signals across the membrane.
  - Drugs analogous to GLP1 exist that activate GLP1 R in a more potent way; keeping
    GLP1-R activated longer, ultimately leading to more insulin release.
